# Ornith 1.0 9B UD-Q4_K_XL on an RTX 3070 Laptop (8 GB) — measured profile
#
# Derived from ornith-35b.env: same architecture family (qwen35, hybrid),
# different size class and a much smaller card. The CTX sweep below WAS run on
# this machine; see the note about gguf-info.py undershooting.

# --- Where the .gguf files live on the host ---
MODELS_DIR=/home/nromero/models

# --- Model ---
# unsloth/Ornith-1.0-9B-GGUF — 5.98 GB, MIT licensed. Multimodal (there is an
# mmproj-*.gguf in the repo), but served text-only here: the projector costs
# ~877 MiB and this card has no room for it.
MODEL_FILE=Ornith-1.0-9B-UD-Q4_K_XL.gguf
MODEL_ALIAS=ornith-9b
CONTAINER_NAME=ornith9b
PORT=8080

# --- Memory ---
# MEASURED on this card, not estimated. A CTX sweep with the container
# restarted at each value gave, as VRAM in use at idle:
#     16384 -> 5,783 MiB     65536 -> 6,839 MiB
#     32768 -> 6,135 MiB     98304 -> 7,543 MiB     131072 -> OOM
# That is 704 MiB per 32,768 tokens = 22.0 KiB/token, which is 29% MORE than
# the 17.0 KiB/token scripts/gguf-info.py computes. The tool gets the KV cache
# itself exactly right (the server confirms 2,176 MiB at 131,072 cells over 8
# layers); the extra ~5 KiB/token is context-dependent buffers the formula does
# not model. Size from the measurement, not from the tool, on a tight card.
#
# 65536 leaves 1,353 MiB free. 98304 works but leaves only 635 MiB, and on this
# laptop the RTX also drives the external monitors — plugging one in eats into
# that. 131072 dies with `cudaMalloc failed: out of memory` on the compute
# buffers, and NOT gracefully: see the SPEC_TYPE note about -ngl and auto-fit.
#
# Raising the context costs VRAM and nothing else: a thermally-controlled sweep
# found no decode penalty from 16k to 98k (the apparent 58.4 -> 56.4 t/s decline
# was the GPU heating from 59 to 86 C; re-running the FIRST config hot gave
# 56.5, reproducing the whole effect with the context unchanged).
CTX=65536
NGL=all
KV_TYPE=q8_0

# --- Sampling: from the Ornith 1.0 9B model card ---
# The card states outright: "Recommended sampling parameters: temperature=0.6,
# top_p=0.95, top_k=20 (use temperature=1.0 to reproduce the reported benchmark
# setup)." So these are Qwen3's values, NOT the temp 1.0 / top_k 0 that
# docs/profiles/ornith-35b.env carries — those came from a hand-configured
# deployment, and the 35B card makes no sampling recommendation at all.
# Do not copy sampling between sizes of the same family either.
TEMP=0.6
TOP_P=0.95
TOP_K=20
MIN_P=0.0
REASONING_FORMAT=deepseek

# --- Throughput ---
# This machine has 62 GB of RAM, against the 27 GB of the reference box, so the
# host-RAM prompt cache can be far more generous than the 10240 used there.
# Still host RAM, not VRAM: check `free -g` before raising it further.
CACHE_RAM=16384

BATCH=2048
UBATCH=512

# --- Speculative decoding ---
# NOT draft-mtp, and this one is worth reading carefully. The upstream
# config.json reports mtp_num_hidden_layers: 1, i.e. the ORIGINAL model does
# ship MTP heads — but gguf-info.py against this quantization reports
# "MTP heads (nextn.*): 0". Unsloth's conversion drops them. That is why
# third-party repos with "MTP" in the name exist for this model.
# So draft-mtp is unavailable here despite the base model having the heads:
# the config of the original is not evidence about the file you downloaded.
# ngram-simple earned almost nothing on the 35B (1.07 tokens per forward pass);
# measuring SPEC_TYPE=none against it is the first experiment to run here.
SPEC_TYPE=ngram-simple
SPEC_N_MAX=8
SPEC_P_MIN=0.7

# --- Exposure ---
# Loopback only. No authentication anywhere in this stack. README section 7.
BIND=127.0.0.1
